+## Boundary -- what this result did NOT establish
+
+- The order of events: code, pull request, then this record. No approval preceded the
+  code except the owner's word to start fixing issue 50, and no reader other than the
+  session that wrote it has reviewed the diff.
+- `--strict` checks that someone answered for a component's entry. It does not check that
+  the answer is right: a `reread:` line can be written without reading anything.
+- A subsystem's `reread:` line can be left unanswered for good. Nothing fails on it and
+  `review` does not date a subsystem.
+- The change was not run on a project that already gates on `changed --strict`, nor on the
+  project the issue came from. What it costs such a project on its next change is not
+  measured.
